Here's an example in JavaScript (which is quite similar in many languages):

```javascript
// Define your regex pattern
const regexPattern = /your_regex_pattern/;

// Function to use the regex
function checkRegex(input) {
    return new RegExp(regexPattern).test(input);
}

// Example usage:
const userInput = "Your input here";
const prefixedInput = `${regexPattern} ${userInput}`;

console.log(checkRegex(prefixedInput));  // This will pass if 'your_regex_pattern' matches user_input.
```

